# The report the eight-request diagnostic wrote. This is the only place the
# masked response excerpts are kept -- §4 of the document above puts them here
# and nowhere else, so if this file is not committed the excerpts exist only in
# a CI artifact that expires. Held by
# tests/test_audio_format_failure_diagnostic.py.
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/335-audio-format-diagnostic.json
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/336-silence-is-not-agreement.md
# 334's stability figures recomputed after the counting fix. 334's own artifact
# is unchanged, so this file is the *only* place the corrected numbers exist --
# if it is not committed, the published figures stay the only figures and the
# correction lives nowhere. Held by tests/test_silence_is_not_agreement.py.
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/336-334-stability-reanalysed.json
# The two documents that take 334 §10's fourth item. 337 pre-registers a
# ten-call format pilot for a candidate observation header; 338 pre-registers
# the comparison that only gets bought if the pilot passes. Both are read at
# run time, not just by people: the measurer takes the sample, the repeat count
# and the diagnostic kind out of the file it is handed, and refuses a run whose
# document does not name them. An uncommitted pre-registration is a run held to
# a file that is not in the checkout. Held by
# tests/test_audio_accuracy_probe_knows_its_own_answers.py.
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/337-format-safe-observation-pilot.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/338-format-safe-observation-ab.md
# What the pilot bought. Ten paid calls, and the artifact is the only place
# the per-call record exists -- the CI artifact expires, and the pilot is not
# run again, so a number that is not committed here is a number nobody can
# ever check. The delivery file is separate because it answers a separate
# question: whether the audio left this process, which a failing arm makes it
# tempting to assume away. Held by tests/test_the_sentence_that_changed_nothing.py.
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/337-audio-accuracy-measured.json
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/337-audio-accuracy-measured-delivery.json
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/339-the-sentence-that-changed-nothing.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/340-we-have-not-seen-audio-metering.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/341-what-a-refused-call-costs.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/342-audio-cost-metering-prereg.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/343-audio-metering-rehearsal.md
!tasks/rebuilding_grading_task/344-the-order-with-no-destination.md

# The grading run writes a sqlite mirror of the cost ledger beside every grade
# file. The published record is the .jsonl next to it; the database is a local
# working copy, tens of megabytes of it. The workflow only ever stages the two
# files it names, but a hand-published result is staged by hand -- as in #322 --
# so the by-product is named here rather than left to whoever is typing.
data/grades/**/*.cost_ledger.sqlite3

